# The pinned teams-for-linux release (ADR 0020).
#
# build/scripts/54-teams.sh downloads exactly this version and refuses to
# continue unless the artefact matches TEAMS_DEB_SHA256. Both values are
# rewritten together by:
#
#     scripts/maintenance/update-teams-for-linux.sh
#
# Do not edit the checksum by hand. A version bumped without its checksum fails
# the build, which is the intended behaviour — the alternative is installing an
# unverified 108 MiB binary from the internet into the immutable host.
#
# This is the one application the image takes OFF Flathub on purpose: the
# Flatpak cannot read /etc/teams-for-linux/config.json, which is where the
# company background service is configured. Moving it here means Teams now
# updates on the image cadence, so a pin left alone is a Teams client left
# behind — check-teams-for-linux.sh says so in CI.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/IsmaelMartinez/teams-for-linux/releases
TEAMS_VERSION=2.20.1
TEAMS_DEB_SHA256=62ee5733dc35cfad84ecc6fe15f09fd74e518ec91eefd0759bae60c775e74d8d
